# Codex GitHub Operation Rules

This repository uses a restricted GitHub proxy.

Do not use GitHub personal access tokens, `GH_TOKEN`, `GITHUB_TOKEN`, or stored GitHub CLI authentication.

Use the provided restricted `gh` shim for GitHub issue and pull request operations.

Allowed commands:

```bash
gh issue create --repo OWNER/REPO --title "..." --body "..."
gh issue edit NUMBER --repo OWNER/REPO --title "..." --body "..." --state open|closed
gh issue comment NUMBER --repo OWNER/REPO --body "..."
gh pr create --repo OWNER/REPO --title "..." --body "..." --head BRANCH --base BRANCH
gh pr edit NUMBER --repo OWNER/REPO --title "..." --body "..." --state open|closed --base BRANCH
```

Forbidden commands:

```bash
gh auth token
gh auth login
gh auth status
gh api
gh pr merge
gh pr checkout
gh pr list
gh pr view
git push
```

The `gh` command in this environment is not the official GitHub CLI. It is a restricted shim that sends allowed Issue/PR operations to the Cloud Run GitHub proxy.

If a required GitHub operation is not supported by the restricted shim, stop and explain the missing operation instead of trying to bypass the proxy.
